{
    "background_story": "Dexter was a devout musician and poet who lived in ancient Israel. He spent most of his days studying the scriptures and composing hymns that reflected his deep love for God. As a psalmist, Dexter's music was not just a form of artistic expression, but a way to connect with the divine. He would often play his lyre on the hills overlooking the city, singing songs of praise and thanksgiving. Dexter's most famous composition, 'Psalm of the Dawn', was said to have been inspired by a breathtaking sunrise over the mountains. His music became a source of comfort and inspiration for the community, and his psalms were often sung in the temple during sacred rituals. Dexter's legacy lived on through his music, which continued to uplift and inspire generations to come.",
